{"baseline":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":123.68,"success_pct":1},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [deep-agent/reliability-model/deepseek-v4-flash] timeout_bug -- RunCommandInJob uses INFINITE wait (WaitForSingleObject with INFINITE) for the job process. If the spawned command hangs indefinitely, the background thread reading stdout/stderr will also hang forever, leaking the thread and the file handle to the log file. There is no timeout parameter exposed to the caller. | Recommend: Add a configurable timeout parameter (default e.g. 24 hours) to RunCommandInJob. After the timeout, terminate the job object via TerminateJobObject and close the log stream. Expose this timeout in the PowerShell wrapper function.","commit":"2684b25c2303bd36d7c531f30d81172e3115bde6","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-06-04T04:42:38.1330649Z"}
