{"baseline":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":154.57,"success_pct":1},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [qa-hardening 1/3] BRIDGE AUDIT SYSTEM HARDENING ATOM 1/3 - fix audit filing/status truthfulness in tools/audit.ps1.\n\nContext from operator audit:\n- Latest audit report found 16 critical findings but filed_to_backlog/backlog_added was 0.\n- audit.log repeated: \"audit backlog Add-Idea filing failed: Add-Idea not recognized\".\n- Suspected root: Initialize-AuditBacklogHelpers dot-sources common.ps1 inside function scope; Add-Idea is then unavailable inside the later filing closure.\n- Also deep-audit can return JSON with every model agent status=error/empty_llm_reply while final audit status still says ok.\n\nRequired implementation:\n1. Make audit backlog filing reliable in the actual filing scope. Direct invocation of tools/audit.ps1 must have Add-Idea/Get-BacklogPath available where Add-AuditCriticalsToBacklog and Add-DeepAuditFindingsToBacklog call them.\n2. Add/extend tests so this exact regression is caught: helper reports available AND a synthetic critical can be filed through Add-AuditCriticalsToBacklog in a temp bridge/channel without Add-Idea scope loss.\n3. Make report status truthful: if required deep agents all fail, or any required deep slice returns empty_llm_reply, final status must become partial/deep_failed (not ok) and errors must include a clear reason. Preserve successful static report generation.\n4. Add metadata counters: deep_agent_success_count, deep_agent_error_count, deep_agent_required_failures if practical.\n\nAcceptance:\n- ParseFile for tools/audit.ps1.\n- Run tools/test-audit-context.ps1, tools/test-audit-decompose.ps1, tools/test-backlog-intake-gate.ps1.\n- Add a focused regression test if existing tests do not cover the direct Add-Idea filing path.\n- Run smoke.ps1.\n- Commit atom with clear message.","commit":"eea78a0f352a55b81521ab836bac386662678689","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-06-04T20:14:26.1701217Z"}
