{"baseline":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":153.8,"success_pct":1},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [qa-hardening 2/3] BRIDGE AUDIT SYSTEM HARDENING ATOM 2/3 - reduce false criticals in tools/audit-security.ps1.\n\nContext from operator audit:\n- Latest report flagged command-injection/hardcoded-credentials inside regex strings and test fixtures, e.g. lib/backlog-workpack.ps1 regex lines and tools/test-backlog-intake-gate.ps1 fixture strings.\n- Current scanner is too raw-line regex based and treats comments/strings/test fixtures as exploitable code.\n\nRequired implementation:\n1. Make command-injection and hardcoded-secret checks token/AST aware enough to ignore comments and string literals that merely contain patterns such as Invoke-Expression, iex, password, secret, token.\n2. Preserve real positives: actual Invoke-Expression/iex command usage in executable code must still be reported; actual hardcoded secret assignments in executable code must still be reported.\n3. Exclude or downgrade intentional test fixtures under tools/test-*.ps1 from critical security filing unless executable production code is actually dangerous.\n4. Keep the scanner conservative for real bridge code, but stop turning audit\u0027s own verifier/test text into critical tasks.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Add a focused test script, for example tools/test-audit-security-precision.ps1, with fixtures for: comment-only secret, string-only regex containing iex, test fixture text, real Invoke-Expression, real secret assignment.\n- ParseFile for tools/audit-security.ps1 and the new test.\n- Run the new test plus tools/test-backlog-intake-gate.ps1 and smoke.ps1.\n- Commit atom with clear message.","commit":"9b816dc93f47dac8437ee0397f045d9fe71a7263","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-06-04T20:27:37.4340980Z"}
