{"delta":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":-41.4,"success_pct":-0.022},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [task-distribution-hardening 2/3] [Packer Guard Fix] Fix workpack classification so negative instructions do not become edit targets.\n\nProblem observed by operator: a task that said protected files were only examples / exclusions was classified as protected-dominant because the packer treated those mentioned paths as touch targets.\n\nGoal: harden classification so text like \"do not edit X\", \"forbidden X\", \"read-only context X\", \"exclude X\", or explicit FORBIDDEN_FILES/READ_ONLY_CONTEXT does not put X into touch_set, conflict_group, or protected lane.\n\nRequired behavior:\n- Add regression coverage for a task whose only editable file is tools/deep-audit-agent.ps1 while forbidden/read-only context mentions protected/control paths.\n- That regression must classify as non-protected audit/tools work, not protected-dominant, not safety lane, and not touch protected/control paths.\n- Keep protected classification when a task positively asks to edit protected/control-plane files.\n- Do not weaken real safety/admission gates.\n\nEXPECTED_FILES:\n- lib/backlog-workpack.ps1\n- tools/test-workpack-batch.ps1 or tools/test-workpack-scope-contract.ps1\n\nFORBIDDEN_FILES:\n- supervisor.ps1\n- watchdog.ps1\n- server.ps1\n- driver.ps1\n- control/*\n\nAcceptance:\n- Regression test fails before fix and passes after fix.\n- Existing protected/control-plane tests still pass.\n- tools/test-workpack-batch.ps1 passes, or explain precisely if a narrower test is used plus why.\n- smoke.ps1 passes.","after_turns":363,"after":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":132.49,"success_pct":0.978},"hypothesis_ts":"2026-06-05T12:34:52.3867217Z","type":"verdict","verdict":"worked","ts":"2026-06-06T23:00:11.3518756Z","commit":"0e32518e0c37cebfedc6fe56791c45e568af7746"}
