{"delta":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":-42.1,"success_pct":-0.0222},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [OPERATOR PREFLIGHT APPROVED: implement commit-worthiness filtering only. Do not reduce QA, critic, smoke, rollback, safety, collect-commit, or normal auto-commit for real code/config/test/doc changes.]\n\n[task-distribution-hardening 3/3] [Telemetry Commit Fix] Stop creating noisy telemetry-only auto-commits.\n\nProblem observed by operator: after a real collect-commit, the driver created a separate auto-commit that contained only channels/main/task-management-shadow.jsonl telemetry. This is not dangerous, but it pollutes git history and confuses review because HEAD no longer points at the code-changing commit.\n\nGoal: prevent auto-commit from committing only runtime/channel telemetry or shadow files, while preserving commits for real code/config/test/documentation changes.\n\nRequired behavior:\n- Diagnose the auto-commit pipeline and add a deterministic filter for commit-worthy paths.\n- If the only dirty paths are channel/runtime telemetry such as channels/*/task-management-shadow.jsonl or similar shadow/log/jsonl runtime files, do not create an auto-commit.\n- If there is at least one real code/config/test/doc change, commit as before; telemetry may be included only if the existing pipeline intentionally includes all dirty files and that is safe, but it must not create a telemetry-only commit.\n- Do not disable normal auto-commit, collect-commit, QA, critic, rollback, or safety behavior.\n\nEXPECTED_FILES:\n- inspect and choose the minimal commit pipeline files needed\n- add or update a focused test if practical\n\nFORBIDDEN_FILES:\n- supervisor.ps1\n- watchdog.ps1\n- server.ps1\n- control/*\n\nAcceptance:\n- Add a test or self-test proving telemetry-only dirty state is skipped.\n- Add a test or self-test proving real code/test/doc dirty state remains commit-worthy.\n- ParseFile passes for changed ps1 files.\n- smoke.ps1 passes.\n- Final report names the exact dirty path patterns excluded from telemetry-only commits.","after_turns":360,"after":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":132.01,"success_pct":0.9778},"hypothesis_ts":"2026-06-05T12:51:54.9553128Z","type":"verdict","verdict":"worked","ts":"2026-06-06T23:00:12.4679494Z","commit":"65aa3ee7406484d1640ea29f91eade3db5f15098"}
